.TH geectl-changelog-validate 1  "geectl-changelog-validate 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-changelog\-validate \- Validate the `.changes` entries in a package directory against the V1–V12 rules. Local\-only by default; with `\-\-target\-project`/`\-\-target\-package` the target\-relative rules (V2, V4, V5 newest\-vs\-target, V11 older entries) run against the target\*(Aqs current files. Exits non\-zero naming the failing rule
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl changelog validate\fR [\fB\-\-target\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-target\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-entries\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIDIR\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Validate the `.changes` entries in a package directory against the V1–V12 rules. Local\-only by default; with `\-\-target\-project`/`\-\-target\-package` the target\-relative rules (V2, V4, V5 newest\-vs\-target, V11 older entries) run against the target\*(Aqs current files. Exits non\-zero naming the failing rule
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-project\fR \fI<TARGET_PROJECT>\fR
The target project to compare against
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-package\fR \fI<TARGET_PACKAGE>\fR
The target package to compare against
.TP
\fB\-\-entries\fR \fI<ENTRIES>\fR [default: 1]
Newest N entries to lint for format, and the number of new entries the submission may carry vs the target (default 1: one entry per SR)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIDIR\fR] [default: .]
The package directory (default: the current directory)
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
